			"notes": "## 📢 Voxy now explains itself in the Sodium settings screen\n\nAfter the `GL_ARB_gpu_shader_int64` gate in `beb06bc8`, unsupported GPUs\ndisabled voxy at startup — and the settings page simply **did not appear**.\nNo tab, no message, nothing. This release fixes that UX dead end.\n\n### What you see now\n\nOpen Sodium's settings (`O` → Video Settings). Voxy always gets a tab.\nOn unsupported hardware it reads:\n\n**Voxy installed — this GPU is not compatible** · `Not supported`\n\nHover it for the full explanation:\n\n```\nVoxy is installed and loaded, but it cannot render on this graphics card.\n\nVoxy has been disabled automatically.\n\nReason: no GL_ARB_gpu_shader_int64          ← names the actual missing capability\n\nVoxy needs a discrete GPU with GL_ARB_gpu_shader_int64 (64-bit integers\nin GLSL). NVIDIA and modern AMD implement it; Intel integrated graphics\ndoes not, even when reporting OpenGL 4.6.\n\nFor LOD rendering on integrated graphics, use Distant Horizons instead.\n```\n\nThe reason line is not hardcoded — `VoxyClient` records which capability\nactually failed, so it says `no compute shader support`,\n`no indirect draw parameters` or `broken depth sampler` when those are\nthe blocker instead.\n\n### Implementation note\n\nSodium 0.6.x exposes only four control types (`TickBoxControl`,\n`SliderControl`, `CyclingControl`) and `OptionImpl.getControl()` is\ndereferenced while drawing every row, so there is no way to render a bare\nlabel row. The notice is therefore a `CyclingControl` over a single-value\nenum, permanently disabled via `setEnabled(false)` — it renders as a\ngreyed-out \"Not supported\" entry and cannot be clicked into a wrong state.\n\nAll strings live in `assets/voxy/lang/en_us.json`, so they are\ntranslatable.\n\n## 📦 Install\n\n**`voxy-0.2.7-alpha.jar` — 822,091 bytes.**\n\n| Asset | Size | Use when |\n|---|---|---|\n| `voxy-0.2.7-alpha.jar` | **822,091 B** | Normal install |\n| `voxy-0.2.7-alpha-all.jar` | 85,119,292 B | Only with RocksDB / Zstd-Storage backends |\n\nRequires Minecraft `1.21.1`, NeoForge `21.1.173`, Sodium.\n\n> ⚠️ Delete every previous `voxy*.jar` before installing. Two Voxy jars\n> ship `com.github.luben.zstd` and Java's module system rejects the\n> duplicate (`Modules lss and com.github.luben.zstd_jni export package …`).\n> `voxy-server-side` belongs on a dedicated **server**.\n\n## Changelog\n\n- `7face4a8` — settings screen explains unsupported GPUs\n- `beb06bc8` — gate voxy on `GL_ARB_gpu_shader_int64` (fixes 19,364 GL errors/session)"
