			"notes": "## 🐛 Intel-iGPU fix — Voxy now disables itself instead of spamming 19,000 GL errors\n\n**Found in production:** a real Prism Launcher 11.1.1 session on an\nIntel Iris Xe (i5-1335U, Windows 11) produced **19,364**\n`GL_INVALID_OPERATION` errors in a single launch. The mod appeared to\n\"work\" — no crash, no visible failure — while every LoD shader silently\nfailed.\n\n### Root cause\n\nVoxy's core LoD shaders require `GL_ARB_gpu_shader_int64` (64-bit integers\nin GLSL):\n\n| Shader | Uses `uint64_t` |\n|---|---|\n| `lod/gl46/cmdgen.comp` | ✅ |\n| `lod/gl46/buildtranslucents.comp` | ✅ |\n| `lod/gl46/quads2.vert` | ✅ |\n| `lod/gl46/quads3.vert` | ✅ |\n| `lod/gl46/cull/raster.vert` | ✅ |\n| `lod/gl46/test/raw.vert` | ✅ |\n| `lod/quad_format.glsl` | ✅ |\n\n`Capabilities` already probed this correctly — `INT64_t` is set by an\nactual shader-compile test, not a flag guess. But **`VoxyClient` never\nread the field.** The gate only checked `compute`, `indirectParameters`\nand `hasBrokenDepthSampler`:\n\n```java\n// before — INT64_t silently ignored\nboolean systemSupported = Capabilities.INSTANCE.compute\n    && Capabilities.INSTANCE.indirectParameters\n    && !Capabilities.INSTANCE.hasBrokenDepthSampler;\n```\n\nIntel iGPUs report **GL 4.6.0** yet do not implement the extension, so\nthey passed every check. Result:\n\n```\nGL error: GLSL compile failed for shader 147:\n  '#extension' : 'GL_ARB_gpu_shader_int64' is not supported\n  'uint64_t' : undeclared identifier\n```\n\n…followed by one `GL_INVALID_OPERATION` per dispatch, forever.\n\n### The fix — `beb06bc8`\n\n`INT64_t` now participates in the gate. Unsupported hardware disables\nVoxy once, with a message that says what to do:\n\n```\nGPU does not support GL_ARB_gpu_shader_int64 (uint64_t in GLSL).\nVoxy's LoD shaders require it and cannot run on this GPU. Disabling voxy.\nThis is a hardware limitation, not a configuration problem.\nIntel integrated GPUs do not implement the extension even at GL 4.6.\n```\n\nOverride for drivers that misreport the capability:\n\n```\n-Dvoxy.forceInt64=true\n```\n\n### Verified\n\n- `./gradlew build` → exit 0\n- Gate logic exercised against the exact Iris Xe capability values read\n  from the log: `forceInt64=false` → disabled, `forceInt64=true` → enabled\n- Fix confirmed present in the shipped `.class` (strings extracted from\n  the built jar)\n\n## 📦 Install\n\n**Download `voxy-0.2.7-alpha.jar` — 819,275 bytes.**\n\n| Asset | Size | Use it when |\n|---|---|---|\n| `voxy-0.2.7-alpha.jar` | **819,275 B** | Normal install |\n| `voxy-0.2.7-alpha-all.jar` | 85,116,476 B | Only with RocksDB / Zstd-Storage backends (ships `rocksdbjni` 78 MB, `zstd-jni` 6 MB, `jedis`, `commons-pool2`, `xz`) |\n\nRequires Minecraft `1.21.1`, NeoForge `21.1.173`, Sodium.\n\n> ⚠️ Delete any previous `voxy*.jar` before dropping in the new one.\n> Multiple Voxy jars in `mods/` cause JPMS split-package failures\n> (`Modules lss and com.github.luben.zstd_jni export package …`).\n> `voxy-server-side` belongs on a **dedicated server**, not beside the\n> client jar.\n\n## ❗ Hardware requirement\n\n**Voxy needs a discrete GPU.** The LoD pipeline depends on\n`GL_ARB_gpu_shader_int64`, which AMD and NVIDIA implement but Intel\nintegrated graphics does not — at any GL version.\n\n| GPU | Works |\n|---|---|\n| NVIDIA RTX / GTX (Compute ≥ 6.0) | ✅ |\n| AMD RX (Vega and newer) | ✅ |\n| AMD Radeon 400/500 (older) | ⚠️ broken depth sampler, disabled by guard |\n| Intel Arc discrete | ❓ untested |\n| Intel Iris Xe / UHD (integrated) | ❌ no `gpu_shader_int64` |\n\nOn integrated graphics, **Distant Horizons** provides comparable LOD\nrendering and does work there."
		},
