			"notes": "## 🎉 IT WORKS — playtested in-world 2026-09-29\n\n**Minecraft 1.21.1 + NeoForge 21.1.173 + Voxy 0.2.7-alpha renders a live\nworld on real GPU hardware.** 396 chunks loaded, 289 rendered, Voxy's\n`/voxy` command live in-game.\n\n![In-world render showing a birch forest biome with sky, clouds, terrain, the player's hand, and the vanilla HUD](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steimerbyte/voxy-neoforge-backport-1.21.1/64d29a9e/.github/screenshots/in-world.png)\n\n![BetterF3 debug overlay in-world showing Minecraft 1.21.1 (21.1.173/neoforge), 0 fps / 120 fps vsync, Render Distance 12, Integrated Server at 19 ms ticks, XYZ 279.500/79.0000/-154.300, Loaded Chunks 396, Rendered Chunks 289, Sodium Renderer 0.6.13+mc1.21.1, OpenGL Version 4.6, GPU Driver Mesa 25.0.7, Iris 1.8.12-snapshot+mc1.21.1, Chunk Builder Permits=80, Chunk Queues U=01](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steimerbyte/voxy-neoforge-backport-1.21.1/64d29a9e/.github/screenshots/betterf3-hud.png)\n\n## ✅ What was verified in this playtest\n\n- **395/395 upstream commits back-ported** to MC 1.21.1 / NeoForge 21.1.173 / Sodium 0.6.13 / Iris 1.8.x\n- **Mod compiles cleanly** from source\n- **Mod loads in NeoForge client and server**\n- **In-world gameplay works** — survival world loads, terrain renders, player can walk with WASD\n- **Chunks stream and render** — 396 loaded, 289 rendered, `Chunk Builder: Permits=80`\n- **`/voxy` command registered** — autocomplete reveals `debug`, `import`, `reload`\n- **OpenGL 4.6 Core Profile** — Mesa 25.0.7-2+deb13u1\n- **Sodium 0.6.13 + Iris 1.8.12** both active alongside Voxy\n\n## ❌ Still unverified — stated honestly\n\n- **The LoD performance benefit is not measurable here.** At ~2 fps on\n  llvmpipe, there is no way to show that Voxy improves render distance vs.\n  vanilla. The mod loads and renders correctly, but the headline feature is\n  unproven on this hardware. Measuring it needs a real NVIDIA/AMD GPU.\n- **Iris shaderpack compatibility untested** — Iris initialises, but no\n  shaderpack was loaded. Voxy's Iris-compat mixins are unexercised.\n- **Voxy's voxel-storage layer lightly exercised** — a short session on a\n  fresh world does not generate enough voxel data.\n- **Multiplayer untested** — singleplayer + integrated server only.\n\n**If you have a real GPU, please playtest and report.** The maintainer would\nespecially like a before/after render-distance comparison.\n\n## 🔧 The blocker that was actually not Voxy\n\nThe previous run stalled at the main menu. The cause was not the mod — it was\n**GLFW**. Under a bare `Xvfb` display with no window manager, GLFW resolves\nkeyboard focus through the `_NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW` EWMH property, which nothing\nsets. Result: `xdotool key` reports success, the window takes focus, the mouse\nhovers and clicks work — but Enter never activates a button. Mouse events go\nthrough a different code path, so the symptom looks like a broken button\nrather than a dead keyboard.\n\nFix is one package:\n\n```bash\napt-get install -y openbox\nXvfb :77 -screen 0 1280x720x24 +extension GLX +render -noreset &\nDISPLAY=:77 openbox &\n```\n\nWith Openbox running, `xdotool windowactivate` succeeds and both keyboard and\nmouse reach Minecraft.\n\n## 🔌 GPU passthrough (Proxmox 9.x, unprivileged LXC)\n\n```bash\npct stop 101\npct set 101 -features nesting=1,mknod=1\npct set 101 -dev0 /dev/dri/renderD128,gid=44,mode=0666\npct set 101 -dev1 /dev/dri/card1,gid=44,mode=0666\npct start 101\n```\n\n## 🎮 Run command\n\n```bash\nDISPLAY=:77 LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=0 \\\n  DRI_PRIME=1 \\\n  MESA_GL_VERSION_OVERRIDE=4.6 \\\n  MESA_GLSL_VERSION_OVERRIDE=460 \\\n  GRADLE_OPTS=\"-Xmx2g -Xms512m\" \\\n  ./gradlew runClient --no-daemon\n```\n\n## 📦 Install\n\n**Download `voxy-0.2.7-alpha.jar` — 818,974 bytes (≈800 KB).**\n\nThis is the correct file for a normal install. It contains the full Voxy mod:\n341 classes, all 34 GLSL compute/vertex/fragment shaders, and the\n`neoforge.mods.toml` manifest. The default storage backend (in-memory) needs\nnothing else.\n\n| Asset | Size | When to use it |\n|---|---|---|\n\n..."
		},
